|---|---|---|---|---|
| Course-level check, mid-year (week 11; it stands for unit 2's end-of-unit assessment) | 2 | 1 | 1 | Day 11 scores unit 2 in full with unseen items and samples unit 1. Unit 2: from a new pictured task (a drawing of a fence: post, rail, repeat), each child lays a step-card algorithm with a start card, a sequence and one repeat (E2-ALG-PS-01); spoken, from a new classroom rule picture (the helper is always the child who sits nearest the door), whether it is fair, with one of the three tests as the reason (E2-ALG-IM-03). Unit 1 sampled: a new part card sorted input or output and placed on the system-diagram (E2-SYS-HW-11) and a new pretend-page card: what happens next (E2-SYS-SE-12); unit 1's end-of-unit record for E2-SYS-IM-13 is carried unscored. Whole-class paper task of about 15 minutes, spoken answers heard in five groups of six. Day 12, the respond day for unit 2 and the check, reteaches by error letter and gathers fresh evidence on the missed items |
| Course-level check, year-end (week 26; it stands for unit 4's end-of-unit assessment) | 4 | 1 | 1 | Day 26 scores unit 4 in full with unseen items and samples units 1 to 3. Unit 4: on paper, sort six new data cards into number data and word data in a two-column table and circle how one was collected (E2-DAT-DC-08); circle the way of asking that leaves people out and, spoken, say who and why (E2-DAT-IM-10); spoken, from a new vague prompt, each child refines a question data can answer (E2-DAT-DI-09); from a new uneven training set, circle the new card the sorter will most likely get wrong and say why (E2-ALG-ML-02). Units 1 to 3 sampled with three short new items: the first wrong block in a new program whose repeat runs one time too many (E2-PRO-TR-07), a new piece of information labeled with a name and stays or changes (E2-PRO-VD-05), and a new pretend-page card (E2-SYS-SE-12); unit 3's end-of-unit record, including each child's laid program and spoken steps (E2-PRO-PD-04, E2-PRO-RD-06), is carried unscored. Unit 5 follows in weeks 28 to 32 and is checked by its own end-of-unit assessment. Day 27, the respond day for unit 4 and the check, reteaches and records each child's support and gains for grade 3 |

## Cross-subject

All leans are to grade 2 courses in the same year. Math and ELA grade 2 meet every school day, so their course days
are their school days (data/plans/calendar.csv); this course's day n falls in week n.

### Mathematics, grade 2

| Row | Lean | Used here | Earliest math unit that teaches it | Bridge if math teaches it later |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| g2-algorithm-loops | m2-arrays-equal-addends (2.OA.C.4: equal groups, repeated addition) | Unit 2, sessions 1 to 3 (weeks 7 to 9) | math grade 2 unit 8 (days 132 to 143, weeks 27 to 29) | Math teaches it later. The repeat count stays at 2 to 4 and is counted pass by pass on fingers or a tally, so the unit needs no equal groups or repeated addition; "repeat 3, clap, stomp" is read as three passes, never as a total of six |
| g2-code-loops | m2-arrays-equal-addends (2.OA.C.4) | Unit 3, sessions 2 to 5 (weeks 14 to 17) | math grade 2 unit 8 (days 132 to 143) | Math teaches it later. As above: the step-through run counts each pass of the repeat aloud, and a square's four sides are counted, not multiplied |
