## For the lead

1. **After-core check weeks (calendar pass).** This course's checks sit in weeks 11 and 26, off the grade 2 core
   check weeks 14 to 16, 18 to 20, 28, 29, 31 and 32. data/plans/calendar.csv shows grade 2 week 11 holding health's
   mid-year check and week 26 holding visual arts' and SEL's year-end checks; they stay for the lead's one calendar
   pass across the after-core frames, under the pick in the kindergarten frame's For the lead 1. Week 26 rather than
   27 is chosen so unit 5 has five weeks (Check weeks); if the pass needs week 27, unit 5 loses its respond day or
   session 3 joins session 1, and the lead says which.
2. **Year 3 of the partial base.** The pilot maps Year 1 to kindergarten, so Year 3 is mapped here to grade 2
   (Year 2 is grade 1's). The Year 3 lessons were placed from their titles and unit overviews on the archived pages
   (2026-11-25), not from the lesson files; the placement is checked when the store folder is made (pilot For the
   lead 4). Offered on: "Connecting computers" lessons 4 to 6 (networks) to the grade 3 frame (g3-reach-internet,
   E3-SYS-NT-14), and "Branching databases" lessons 3 to 6 (a yes or no tree, a selection-like structure) to the
   grade 3 frame (g3-attributes or g3-algorithm-combo).
3. **The picture-block editor's repeat.** Pilot For the lead 5 asks for a kindergarten-to-grade-2 picture-block mode
   (scope, Cory's). Grade 2 adds two needs to that ask: an event block and a repeat block whose step-through run counts
   each pass. The paper path meets every grade 2 id in full, so the course does not wait on it.
