r it. Tools: none (all unplugged). Curio Class writes: the dance and drawing step-card sets with start and repeat cards, the line-leader and game rule cards, a short read-aloud about a class that changes how it picks a helper | Second because unit 3's programs are built from these algorithms (g2-code-loops' model_in is the step-card), so the repeat is understood on cards before it is a block. The fairness session sits with the algorithm it judges, and gives unit 4's "who is left out" its first words. Our own (the partial base's Year 3 has no unplugged algorithm unit with repeat) | Candidate: kept, a drawing algorithm (a square) beside the dance for children who cannot do a move, zero added days | Dance moves are done in place, and a child may do any move seated or with hands only; no move is required of a child's body. The fast-runner rule: talk stays on the rule, never on a classmate who is slower or who uses a wheelchair; the teacher picks the game so no child is singled out, and uses the wording the sensitivity read settles from the NCDJ guide. Agent reads: sensitivity. |
